  "name": "@lottiefiles/creator-mcp",
  "readme": "# @lottiefiles/creator-mcp\n\n[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@lottiefiles/creator-mcp.svg?style=flat-square)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@lottiefiles/creator-mcp)\n\nLet AI control [LottieFiles Creator](https://creator.lottiefiles.com?utm_source=npm) \u2014\nbuild and edit Lottie animations through natural language.\n\n<!-- TODO: Add demo GIF showing AI assistant controlling Creator -->\n\n[Getting Started](#getting-started) | [Example Prompts](#example-prompts)\n\n---\n\n## What It Does\n\nThis MCP server connects AI assistants like Claude, Cursor, and Windsurf to the\n[LottieFiles Creator](https://creator.lottiefiles.com?utm_source=npm) animation editor.\nYour AI gets the same native animation tools used by Motion Copilot, so it can read,\nmodify, and create animations on your behalf without executing arbitrary scripts.\n\n- **Read & modify animation properties** \u2014 colors, transforms, opacity, timing\n- **Create shapes, layers, and keyframes** through typed native tools\n- **Inspect animation structure** \u2014 list layers, examine keyframes, export data\n- **Use Creator-native workflows** \u2014 scenes, motion systems, themes, segments, and more\n\n## Getting Started\n\nFollow the\n[Creator MCP tutorial](https://docs.lottiefiles.com/en/creator/13_ai-tools/lottie-creator-mcp)\nfor comprehensive installation and user guides.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- **Node.js** 18 or later\n- **LottieFiles Creator** open in your browser at\n  [creator.lottiefiles.com](https://creator.lottiefiles.com?utm_source=npm)\n- An MCP-compatible AI assistant\n\n### Install\n\n[![Install in VS Code](https://img.shields.io/badge/Install_in-VS_Code-0098FF?style=flat-square&logo=visualstudiocode&logoColor=ffffff)](https://vscode.dev/redirect/mcp/install?name=%40lottiefiles%2Fcreator-mcp&config=%7B%22command%22%3A%22npx%22%2C%22args%22%3A%5B%22-y%22%2C%22%40lottiefiles%2Fcreator-mcp%22%5D%7D)\n[![Install in VS Code Insiders](https://img.shields.io/badge/Install_in-VS_Code_Insiders-24bfa5?style=flat-square&logo=visualstudiocode&logoColor=ffffff)](https://insiders.vscode.dev/redirect/mcp/install?name=%40lottiefiles%2Fcreator-mcp&config=%7B%22command%22%3A%22npx%22%2C%22args%22%3A%5B%22-y%22%2C%22%40lottiefiles%2Fcreator-mcp%22%5D%7D&quality=insiders)\n\nAdd the following config to your MCP client:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"lottiefiles-creator\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### MCP Client configuration\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Amp</strong></summary>\n\n```bash\namp mcp add lottiefiles-creator -- npx -y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Antigravity</strong></summary>\n\nFollow Antigravity's MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Claude Code</strong></summary>\n\n```bash\nclaude mcp add lottiefiles-creator -- npx -y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Claude Desktop</strong></summary>\n\nUse the config above in your `claude_desktop_config.json`.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Cline</strong></summary>\n\nFollow Cline's MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Codex</strong></summary>\n\nFollow the [configure MCP guide](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/docs/config.md)\nusing:\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.lottiefiles-creator]\ncommand = \"npx\"\nargs = [\"-y\", \"@lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\"]\n```\n\nOr add via CLI:\n\n```bash\ncodex mcp add lottiefiles-creator -- npx -y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Copilot CLI</strong></summary>\n\n1. Start `copilot`\n2. Run `/mcp add`\n3. Configure:\n\n- Server name: `lottiefiles-creator`\n- Server type: `Local`\n- Command: `npx -y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Copilot / VS Code</strong></summary>\n\nFollow VS Code MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\nOr via CLI:\n\n```bash\ncode --add-mcp '{\"name\":\"lottiefiles-creator\",\"command\":\"npx\",\"args\":[\"-y\",\"@lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\"]}'\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Copilot / GitHub CLI</strong></summary>\n\n```bash\ngh copilot mcp add lottiefiles-creator -- npx -y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Cursor</strong></summary>\n\nUse the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Factory CLI</strong></summary>\n\n```bash\ndroid mcp add lottiefiles-creator \"npx -y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\"\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Gemini CLI</strong></summary>\n\n```bash\ngemini mcp add lottiefiles-creator npx -y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\ngemini mcp add -s user lottiefiles-creator npx -y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Gemini Code Assist</strong></summary>\n\nFollow Gemini Code Assist MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>JetBrains AI Assistant & Junie</strong></summary>\n\nFollow JetBrains MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Kiro</strong></summary>\n\nFollow Kiro MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Qoder</strong></summary>\n\nFollow Qoder MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Visual Studio</strong></summary>\n\nAdd a local MCP server with:\n\n- Name: `lottiefiles-creator`\n- Command: `npx`\n- Arguments: `-y @lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Warp</strong></summary>\n\nFollow Warp MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Windsurf</strong></summary>\n\nFollow Windsurf MCP setup docs and use the config above.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>VS Code</strong></summary>\n\nIf using `.vscode/mcp.json`, use:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"servers\": {\n    \"lottiefiles-creator\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@lottiefiles/creator-mcp@latest\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### Your first prompt\n\n1. Open [LottieFiles Creator](https://creator.lottiefiles.com?utm_source=npm).\n2. Enable MCP in Creator.\n3. Keep that tab open while using your AI assistant.\n\nAsk your assistant:\n\n```text\nWhat is the active scene size in LottieFiles Creator?\n```\n\nIf setup is correct, you should see a tool response with scene dimensions.\n\n## Example Prompts\n\nOnce connected, try asking your AI assistant:\n\n| Prompt                                         | What it does                                     |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| \"What layers are in this animation?\"           | Lists all layers with their types and properties |\n| \"Change the background color to blue\"          | Modifies the background layer color              |\n| \"List all keyframes on the first layer\"        | Inspects keyframe data for a specific layer      |\n| \"Make the animation loop smoothly\"             | Adjusts timing and easing for seamless looping   |\n| \"Center all selected layers in the scene\"      | Aligns selected layers to scene center           |\n| \"Change all fills to a neon cyan palette\"      | Batch-updates colors across shapes               |\n| \"Create a pulsing loading spinner\"             | Builds a looped shape animation                  |\n| \"Offset each layer by 3 frames\"                | Staggers layer timing for motion rhythm          |\n| \"Remove hidden layers from this scene\"         | Cleans up invisible and unused layers            |\n| \"Round all rectangle corners to 16\"            | Applies consistent corner radius styling         |\n| \"List every text layer and its content\"        | Extracts text content for copy review            |\n| \"Duplicate this scene and make a dark variant\" | Creates an alternate themed scene                |\n| \"Create a 2-second intro with logo fade-in\"    | Generates timeline-based intro animation         |\n\n<!-- TODO: Add screenshot showing example prompt and Creator result side-by-side -->\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
